 "tags": [
  {
   "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon Kinesis Video Streams API (2017-09-30). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Streams and signaling channels are stored records: no media is ingested, stored or played, and no WebRTC signaling, relay or ICE server exists. GetDataEndpoint, GetSignalingChannelEndpoint, the edge agent, media storage, image generation, notification, stream storage and mapped resource configuration APIs return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501, so no endpoint is ever returned. Streams and channels are ACTIVE at once. The ARN ends in the fixed number 1 instead of the creation timestamp AWS uses, so a deleted and recreated name has the same ARN. A stream created without a KmsKeyId reports the alias alias/aws/kinesisvideo instead of the ARN of that managed key; the key is not resolved. StreamStorageConfiguration is refused. Updates require CurrentVersion, which must equal the stored Version or the request fails with VersionMismatchException; every successful update gives the resource a new Version. UpdateDataRetention adds or subtracts the change from the retention in hours, which must stay from 0 to 87600. DeleteStream and DeleteSignalingChannel delete the latest version, or refuse with VersionMismatchException a CurrentVersion that is not the stored Version; ListStreams and ListSignalingChannels refuse the name condition. Only SINGLE_MASTER channels can be created. Tags are read and changed through TagResource, UntagResource and ListTagsForResource by ARN; TagStream, UntagStream and ListTagsForStream are not bound. A tag count above 50 reached through TagResource fails with ClientLimitExceededException and a channel count above the simulator limit fails the same way, because the engine cannot name the more specific modeled exceptions.",
   "name": "Amazon Kinesis Video Streams"
  }
 ],
